# Price and volume on one x-axis

Volume gets its own panel below the price, sharing the x-axis and nothing else.
Overlaid on a shared y it would be the dual-axis anti-pattern in its most common
disguise; stacked, the two measures stay comparable to themselves. The volume
bars are tinted by the period's own direction, and the five-session moving
average is computed by the reader from the same numbers the table carries.

```mdv ohlcv
title: ACME — daily with volume
x: date
volumeHeight: 0.25
volumeColor: direction
precision: 2
overlay:
  - {type: sma, period: 5}
format: table
---
date       |  open |  high |   low | close |  volume
2026-08-03 | 41.20 | 42.05 | 40.90 | 41.85 | 1284000
2026-08-04 | 41.90 | 42.40 | 41.10 | 41.30 | 1642000
2026-08-05 | 41.35 | 41.60 | 39.80 | 40.05 | 2410000
2026-08-06 | 40.10 | 41.75 | 40.00 | 41.60 | 1988000
2026-08-07 | 41.65 | 42.20 | 41.40 | 42.10 | 1146000
2026-08-10 | 42.05 | 43.15 | 41.95 | 43.00 | 1732000
2026-08-11 | 43.10 | 43.40 | 42.30 | 42.55 | 1394000
2026-08-12 | 42.50 | 42.85 | 41.70 | 41.90 | 1208000
2026-08-13 | 41.95 | 42.60 | 41.85 | 42.45 |  976000
2026-08-14 | 42.50 | 43.80 | 42.40 | 43.65 | 2065000
```
